---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
error[reversed_range]: the range `10..0` is empty: ranges count up
  --> tests/lint/reversed_range/bad.jai:5:12
   |
 5 |     for i: 10..0 print("%\n", i);
   |            ^^^^^
   |
help: to count down, write `for < ...: 0..10`
   |
 4       xs := int.[1, 2, 3];
 5 ~     for < i: 0..10 print("%\n", i);
 6       for i: xs.count - 1..0 print("%\n", xs[i]);
   |
   = note: `reversed_range` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/reversed_range

error[reversed_range]: the range `xs.count - 1..0` is empty: ranges count up
  --> tests/lint/reversed_range/bad.jai:6:12
   |
 6 |     for i: xs.count - 1..0 print("%\n", xs[i]);
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
help: to count down, write `for < ...: 0..xs.count - 1`
   |
 5       for i: 10..0 print("%\n", i);
 6 ~     for < i: 0..xs.count - 1 print("%\n", xs[i]);
 7   }
   |
   = note: `reversed_range` is `deny` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/reversed_range
